questions.question:
Consider this EF Core entity:

public class User
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string Username { get; set; } = String.Empty;
    public string HashedPassword { get; set; } = String.Empty;
    public bool IsAdmin { get; set; }
}

Which of the following would be an appropriate DTO to return to a client asking for user details?

options.A:
public class UserDto {
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string Username { get; set; }
}

options.B:
public class UserDto {
    public string HashedPassword { get; set; }
}

options.D:
public class UserDto {
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string Username { get; set; }
    public string HashedPassword { get; set; }
    public bool IsAdmin { get; set; }
}

explanation.questionVi:
Xét thực thể EF Core sau:

public class User
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string Username { get; set; } = String.Empty;
    public string HashedPassword { get; set; } = String.Empty;
    public bool IsAdmin { get; set; }
}

Khai báo DTO nào sau đây là phù hợp nhất để trả về cho client khi họ yêu cầu thông tin chi tiết người dùng?

optionsVi.A:
public class UserDto {
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string Username { get; set; }
}

optionsVi.B:
public class UserDto {
    public string HashedPassword { get; set; }
}

optionsVi.D:
public class UserDto {
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string Username { get; set; }
    public string HashedPassword { get; set; }
    public bool IsAdmin { get; set; }
}

explanation.answerDisplay:
A. public class UserDto {
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string Username { get; set; }
}
